anisotropic charged\ncylinder in the context of $f(R,T)$ theory ($R$ \
represents the Ricci scalar and\n$T$ denotes the trace of energy-momentum \
tensor). For this purpose, we take an\nauxiliary solution of Einstein-Maxwell \
field equations and evaluate expansion\nscalar whose negative values lead to \
collapse and positive values give\nexpansion. For both cases, the behavior of \
density, pressure, anisotropic\nparameter as well as mass is explored and the \
effects of charge as well as\nmodel parameter on these quantities are \
examined. The energy conditions are\nfound to be satisfied for both \
solutions.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Thu, 10 Jan 2019 06:50:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2019-02-19", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Sharif", "M.", ""}, {
               "Siddiqa", "Aisha", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], InsetBox[
