, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The aim of this paper is to reconstruct and analyze \
the stability of some\\ncosmological models against linear perturbations in \
$f(\\\\mathcal{G},T)$ gravity\\n($\\\\mathcal{G}$ and $T$ represent the \
Gauss-Bonnet invariant and trace of the\\nenergy-momentum tensor, \
respectively). We formulate the field equations for\\nboth general as well as \
particular cases in the context of isotropic and\\nhomogeneous universe \
model. We reproduce the cosmic evolution corresponding to\\nde Sitter \
universe, power-law solutions and phantom/non-phantom eras in this\\ntheory \
using reconstruction technique. Finally, we study stability analysis of\\nde \
Sitter as well as power-law solutions through linear perturbations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
