                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this paper, we investigate static spherically \
symmetric wormhole solutions\\nin the background of $F(T,T_\\\\mathcal{G})$ \
gravity ($T$ is the torsion scalar\\nand $T_{\\\\mathcal{G}}$ represents \
teleparallel equivalent of the Gauss-Bonnet\\nterm). We study the wormhole \
solutions by assuming four different matter\\ncontents, a specific redshift \
function and a particular $F(T,T_\\\\mathcal{G})$\\nmodel. The behavior of \
null/weak energy conditions for these fluids is analyzed\\ngraphically. It \
turns out that wormhole solutions can be obtained in the\\nabsence of exotic \
matter for some particular regions of spacetime. We also\\nexplore stability \
of wormhole solutions through equilibrium condition. It is\\nconcluded that \
there exist physically acceptable wormhole solutions for\\nanisotropic, \
isotropic and traceless fluids.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
