                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  This paper is devoted to study the cosmological \
behavior of homogeneous and\\nisotropic universe model in the context of \
$f(R,T^{\\\\varphi})$ gravity where\\n$\\\\varphi$ is the scalar field. For \
this purpose, we follow the first order\\nformalism defined by \
$H=W(\\\\varphi)$. We evaluate Hubble parameter, effective\\nequation of \
state parameter $(\\\\omega^{eff})$, deceleration parameter and\\npotential \
of scalar field for three different values of $W(\\\\varphi)$. We \
obtain\\nphantom era in some cases for the early times. It is found that \
exponential\\nexpression of $W(\\\\varphi)$ yields $\\\\omega^{eff}$ \
independent of time for flat\\nuniverse and independent of model parameter \
otherwise. It is concluded that our\\nmodel corresponds to $\\\\Lambda$CDM \
for both initial as well as late times.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
