$\\mathcal{Q}=\\mathcal{R}_{\\chi\\xi}\\mathcal{T}^{\\chi\\xi}$. We discuss \
the\nphysical features of compact objects by employing bag model equation of \
state\nand construct the modified field equations in terms of Krori-Barua \
ansatz\ninvolving unknowns ($A,B,C$). The observational data of 4U \
1820-30,~Vela\nX-I,~SAX J 1808.4-3658,~RXJ 1856-37 and Her X-I is used to \
calculate these\nunknowns and bag constant $\\mathfrak{B_c}$. Further, we \
observe the behavior of\nenergy density, radial and tangential pressure as \
well as anisotropy through\ngraphical interpretation for a viable model \
$\\mathcal{R}+\\varrho\\mathcal{Q}$ of\nthis gravity. For a particular value \
of the coupling constant $\\varrho$, we\nstudy the behavior of mass, \
compactness, redshift and the energy bounds. The\nstability of the considered \
stars is also checked by using two criteria. We\nconclude that our developed \
structure in this gravity is in well-agreement with\nall the physical \
requirements.\n", 
