          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "gr-qc/0504103", "submitter" -> "Muhammad Sharif", 
             "authors" -> "M. Sharif and Sehar Aziz", "title" -> 
             "Kinematic Self-Similar Cylindrically Symmetric Solutions", 
             "comments" -> 
             "22 pages, accepted for publication in Int. J. of Mod. Phys. D", 
             "journal-ref" -> "Int.J.Mod.Phys. D14 (2005) 1527-1544", "doi" -> 
             "10.1142/S0218271805007115", "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> 
             "gr-qc", "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  This paper is devoted to find out cylindrically symmetric \
kinematic\nself-similar perfect fluid and dust solutions. We study the \
cylindrically\nsymmetric solutions which admit kinematic self-similar vectors \
of second,\nzeroth and infinite kinds, not only for the tilted fluid case but \
also for the\nparallel and orthogonal cases. It is found that the parallel \
case gives\ncontradiction both in perfect fluid and dust cases. The \
orthogonal perfect\nfluid case yields a vacuum solution while the orthogonal \
dust case gives\ncontradiction. It is worth mentioning that the tilted case \
provides solution\nboth for the perfect as well as dust cases.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
