, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  This paper is devoted to study the generalized second \
law of thermodynamics\\nin $f(T)$ gravity. We use quantum corrections such as \
power-law and logarithmic\\ncorrected entropies to the horizon entropy along \
with Gibbs' equation in the\\nthermal equilibrium state. We derive $f(T)$ \
model by taking into account a\\npower-law scale factor through the first \
modified Friedmann equation which\\nobeys the condition for a realistic \
model. Two types of horizons, i.e., Hubble\\nand event horizons are used to \
check the validity of the generalized second law\\nof thermodynamics with \
corrected entropies. We conclude that this law holds\\nwith a specific range \
of entropy parameter on both horizons in the case of\\npower-law corrected \
entropy, while it violates for all values of entropy\\nparameter on both \
horizons for logarithmic corrected entropy.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
