                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  It has been pointed by Hall et al. [1] that matter \
collinations can be\\ndefined by using three different methods. But there \
arises the question of\\nwhether one studies matter collineations by using \
the ${\\\\cal L}_\\\\xi T_{ab}=0$,\\nor ${\\\\cal L}_\\\\xi T^{ab}=0$ or ${\\\
\\cal L}_\\\\xi T_a^b=0$. These alternative\\nconditions are, of course, not \
generally equivalent. This problem has been\\nexplored by applying these \
three definitions to general static spherically\\nsymmetric spacetimes. We \
compare the results with each definition.\\n\""}]}, {
