                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In this paper we classify static plane symmetric \
spacetimes according to\\ntheir matter collineations. These have been studied \
for both cases when the\\nenergy-momentum tensor is non-degenerate and also \
when it is degenerate. It\\nturns out that the non-degenerate case yields \
either {\\\\it four}, {\\\\it five},\\n{\\\\it six}, {\\\\it seven} or \
{\\\\it ten} independent matter collineations in which\\n{\\\\it four} are \
isometries and the rest are proper. There exists three\\ninteresting cases \
where the energy-momentum tensor is degenerate but the group\\nof matter \
collineations is finite-dimensional. The matter collineations in\\nthese \
cases are either {\\\\it four}, {\\\\it six} or {\\\\it ten\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
