, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The collision of black holes and the emission of \
gravitational radiation in\\nhigher-dimensional spacetimes are of interest in \
various research areas,\\nincluding the gauge-gravity duality, the TeV \
gravity scenarios evoked for the\\nexplanation of the hierarchy problem, and \
the large-dimensionality limit of\\ngeneral relativity. We present numerical \
simulations of head-on collisions of\\nnonspinning, unequal-mass black holes \
starting from rest in general relativity\\nwith $4 \\\\leq D\\\\leq 10$ \
spacetime dimensions. We compare the energy and linear\\nmomentum radiated in \
gravitational waves with perturbative predictions in the\\nextreme mass ratio \
limit, demonstrating the strength and limitations of\\nblack-hole \
perturbation theory in this context.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
