Zilhao\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"The physics of black hole binaries: geodesics, \
relaxation modes and\\n  energy extraction\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"6 pages, RevTex4. v2: Addition of Supplemental Material, \
with\\n  substantial further evidence for the universality of binary \
ringdown, and\\n  convergence studies of our numerical results. Accepted in \
Physical Review D\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys. Rev. D 100, 044002 (2019)\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.100.044002\""}]}, {
               
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc astro-ph.HE\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Black holes are the simplest macroscopic objects, and \
provide unique tests of\\nGeneral Relativity. They have been compared to the \
Hydrogen atom in quantum\\nmechanics. Here, we establish a few facts about \
the simplest systems bound by\\ngravity: black hole binaries. We provide \
strong evidence for the existence of\\n`global' photosurfaces surrounding the \
binary, and of binary quasinormal modes\\nleading to exponential decay of \
massless fields when the binary spacetime is\\nslightly perturbed. These two \
properties go hand in hand, as they did for\\nisolated black holes. The \
binary quasinormal modes have high quality factor and\\nmay be prone to \
resonant excitations. Finally, we show that energy extraction\\nfrom binaries \
is generic and we find evidence of a new mechanism -- akin to the\\nFermi \
acceleration process -- whereby the binary transfers energy to \
its\\nsurroundings in a cascading process. The mechanism is conjectured to \
work when\\nthe individual components spin, or are made of compact \
stars.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
