unique tests of\nGeneral Relativity. They have been compared to the Hydrogen \
atom in quantum\nmechanics. Here, we establish a few facts about the simplest \
systems bound by\ngravity: black hole binaries. We provide strong evidence \
for the existence of\n`global' photosurfaces surrounding the binary, and of \
binary quasinormal modes\nleading to exponential decay of massless fields \
when the binary spacetime is\nslightly perturbed. These two properties go \
hand in hand, as they did for\nisolated black holes. The binary quasinormal \
modes have high quality factor and\nmay be prone to resonant excitations. \
Finally, we show that energy extraction\nfrom binaries is generic and we find \
evidence of a new mechanism -- akin to the\nFermi acceleration process -- \
whereby the binary transfers energy to its\nsurroundings in a cascading \
process. The mechanism is conjectured to work when\nthe individual components \
spin, or are made of compact stars.\n", 
