, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We continue our series of studies of high-energy \
collisions of black holes\\ninvestigating unequal-mass, boosted head-on \
collisions in four dimensions. We\\nshow that the fraction of the \
center-of-mass energy radiated as gravitational\\nwaves becomes independent \
of mass ratio and approximately equal to $13\\\\%$ at\\nlarge energies. We \
support this conclusion with calculations using black hole\\nperturbation \
theory and Smarr's zero-frequency limit approximation. These\\nresults lend \
strong support to the conjecture that the detailed structure of\\nthe \
colliding objects is irrelevant at high energies.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
