            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"1102.4352\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Jorge Rocha\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Jorge V. Rocha, Vitor Cardoso\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Gravitational perturbation of the BTZ black hole induced \
by test\\n  particles and weak cosmic censorship in AdS spacetime\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"6 pages, no figures; v2: minor corrections and reference \
added to\\n  match published version\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Rev.D83:104037,2011\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.83.104037\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"gr-qc hep-th\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We analyze the gravitational perturbations induced by \
particles falling into\\na three dimensional, asymptotically AdS black hole \
geometry. More specifically,\\nwe solve the linearized perturbation equations \
obtained from the geodesic\\nmotion of a ring-like distribution of test \
particles in the BTZ background.\\nThis setup ensures that the U(1) symmetry \
of the background is preserved. The\\nnon-asymptotic flatness of the \
background raises difficulties in attributing\\nthe significance of energy \
and angular momentum to the conserved quantities of\\nthe test particles. \
This issue is well known but, to the best of our knowledge,\\nhas never been \
addressed in the literature. We confirm that the naive\\nexpressions for \
energy and angular momentum are the correct definitions.\\nFinally, we put an \
asymptotically AdS version of the weak cosmic censorship to\\na test: by \
attempting to overspin the BTZ black hole with test particles it is\\nfound \
that the black hole cannot be spun-up past its extremal limit.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
