             "Gravitational perturbation of the BTZ black hole induced by \
test\n  particles and weak cosmic censorship in AdS spacetime", "comments" -> 
             "6 pages, no figures; v2: minor corrections and reference added \
to\n  match published version", "journal-ref" -> "Phys.Rev.D83:104037,2011", 
             "doi" -> "10.1103/PhysRevD.83.104037", "report-no" -> Null, 
             "categories" -> "gr-qc hep-th", "license" -> 
             "http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/", 
             "abstract" -> 
             "  We analyze the gravitational perturbations induced by \
particles falling into\na three dimensional, asymptotically AdS black hole \
geometry. More specifically,\nwe solve the linearized perturbation equations \
obtained from the geodesic\nmotion of a ring-like distribution of test \
particles in the BTZ background.\nThis setup ensures that the U(1) symmetry \
of the background is preserved. The\nnon-asymptotic flatness of the \
background raises difficulties in attributing\nthe significance of energy and \
angular momentum to the conserved quantities of\nthe test particles. This \
issue is well known but, to the best of our knowledge,\nhas never been \
addressed in the literature. We confirm that the naive\nexpressions for \
energy and angular momentum are the correct definitions.\nFinally, we put an \
asymptotically AdS version of the weak cosmic censorship to\na test: by \
attempting to overspin the BTZ black hole with test particles it is\nfound \
that the black hole cannot be spun-up past its extremal limit.\n", 
