                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In an earlier paper we studied the \
infinite-dimensional symmetries of\\nsymmetric-space sigma models (SSMs) in a \
flat two-dimensional spacetime. Here,\\nwe extend our investigation to the \
case of two-dimensional SSMs coupled to\\ngravity. These theories arise from \
the toroidal reduction of higher-dimensional\\ngravity and supergravities to \
two dimensions. We construct explicit expressions\\nfor the symmetry \
transformations under the affine Kac-Moody extension $\\\\hat G$\\nthat \
arises when starting from a G/H coset model. We also construct \
further\\nexplicit symmetry transformations that correspond to the modes L_n \
of a\\nVirasoro subalgebra with $n\\\\ge -1$.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
