                  "\"M. Cvetic, H. Lu, C.N. Pope and A. Sadrzadeh\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Consistency of Kaluza-Klein Sphere Reductions of \
Symmetric Potentials\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Latex, 14 pages, minor corrections\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Phys.Rev.D62:046005,2000\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1103/PhysRevD.62.046005\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  In a recent paper, the complete (non-linear) \
Kaluza-Klein Ansatz for the\\nconsistent embedding of certain scalar plus \
gravity subsectors of gauged\\nmaximal supergravity in D=4, 5 and 7 was \
presented, in terms of sphere\\nreductions from D=11 or type IIB \
supergravity. The scalar fields included in\\nthe truncations were the \
diagonal fields in the SL(N,R)/SO(N) scalar\\nsubmanifolds of the full scalar \
sectors of the corresponding maximal\\nsupergravities, with N=8, 6 and 5. The \
embeddings were used for obtaining an\\ninterpretation of extremal D=4, 5 or \
7 AdS domain walls in terms of distributed\\nM-branes or D-branes in the \
higher dimensions. Although strong supporting\\nevidence for the correctness \
of the embedding Ansatze was presented, a full\\nproof of the consistency was \
not given. Here, we complete the proof, by showing\\nexplicitly that the full \
set of higher-dimensional equations of motion are\\nsatisfied if and only if \
the lower-dimensional fields satisfy the relevant\\nscalar plus gravity \
equations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
