           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0002128\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Justin Vazquez-Poritz\""}]}, {
               
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"M. Cvetic, H. Lu and J.F. Vazquez-Poritz\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Absorption by Extremal D3-branes\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Latex, 9 figures and 17 pages\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "\"JHEP 0102:012,2001\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"10.1088/1126-6708/2001/02/012\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  The absorption in the extremal D3-brane background is \
studied for a class of\\nmassless fields whose linear perturbations leave the \
ten-dimensional background\\nmetric unperturbed, as well as the \
minimally-coupled massive scalar. We find\\nthat various fields have the same \
absorption probability as that of the\\ndilaton-axion system, which is given \
exactly via the Mathieu equation. We\\nanalyze the features of the absorption \
cross-sections in terms of effective\\nSchr\\\\\\\"odinger potentials, \
conjecture a general form of the dual effective\\npotentials, and provide \
explicit numerical results for the whole energy range.\\nAs expected, all \
partial-wave absorption probabilities tend to zero (one) at\\nlow (large) \
energies, and exhibit an oscillatory pattern as a function of\\nenergy. The \
equivalence of absorption probabilities for various modes has\\nimplications \
for the correlation functions on the field, including \
subleading\\ncontributions on the field-theory side. In particular, certain \
half-integer and\\ninteger spin fields have identical absorption \
probabilities, thus providing\\nevidence that the corresponding operator \
pairs on the field theory side belong\\nto the same \
supermultiplets.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
