          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "hep-th/0002128", "submitter" -> "Justin Vazquez-Poritz", 
             "authors" -> "M. Cvetic, H. Lu and J.F. Vazquez-Poritz", "title" -> 
             "Absorption by Extremal D3-branes", "comments" -> 
             "Latex, 9 figures and 17 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
             "JHEP 0102:012,2001", "doi" -> "10.1088/1126-6708/2001/02/012", 
             "report-no" -> Null, "categories" -> "hep-th", "license" -> Null,
              "abstract" -> 
             "  The absorption in the extremal D3-brane background is studied \
for a class of\nmassless fields whose linear perturbations leave the \
ten-dimensional background\nmetric unperturbed, as well as the \
minimally-coupled massive scalar. We find\nthat various fields have the same \
absorption probability as that of the\ndilaton-axion system, which is given \
exactly via the Mathieu equation. We\nanalyze the features of the absorption \
cross-sections in terms of effective\nSchr\\\"odinger potentials, conjecture \
a general form of the dual effective\npotentials, and provide explicit \
numerical results for the whole energy range.\nAs expected, all partial-wave \
absorption probabilities tend to zero (one) at\nlow (large) energies, and \
exhibit an oscillatory pattern as a function of\nenergy. The equivalence of \
absorption probabilities for various modes has\nimplications for the \
correlation functions on the field, including subleading\ncontributions on \
the field-theory side. In particular, certain half-integer and\ninteger spin \
fields have identical absorption probabilities, thus providing\nevidence that \
the corresponding operator pairs on the field theory side belong\nto the same \
supermultiplets.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Tue, 15 Feb 2000 23:25:13 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2009-10-31", 
