                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  Little string theories (LSTs) are UV complete \
non-local 6D theories decoupled\\nfrom gravity in which there is an intrinsic \
string scale. In this paper we\\npresent a systematic approach to the \
construction of supersymmetric LSTs via\\nthe geometric phases of F-theory. \
Our central result is that all LSTs with more\\nthan one tensor multiplet are \
obtained by a mild extension of 6D superconformal\\nfield theories (SCFTs) in \
which the theory is supplemented by an additional,\\nnon-dynamical tensor \
multiplet, analogous to adding an affine node to an ADE\\nquiver, resulting \
in a negative semidefinite Dirac pairing. We also show that\\nall 6D SCFTs \
naturally embed in an LST. Motivated by physical considerations,\\nwe show \
that in geometries where we can verify the presence of two \
elliptic\\nfibrations, exchanging the roles of these fibrations amounts to \
T-duality in\\nthe 6D theory compactified on a circle.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
