         TagBox[
          
          TooltipBox[
           DiskBox[{4.3787884374060315`, 0.4061640846339486}, 
            0.05675392870450458],
           TagBox[
            TagBox[
             GridBox[{{
                RowBox[{"\"id\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th/0309208\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"submitter\"", "\[Rule]", "\"Andrei Okounkov\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"authors\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Andrei Okounkov, Nikolai Reshetikhin, Cumrun Vafa\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"title\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Quantum Calabi-Yau and Classical Crystals\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"26 pages, 8 figures; corrected version\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"hep-th math-ph math.MP\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We propose a new duality involving topological strings \
in the limit of large\\nstring coupling constant.\\n  The dual is described \
in terms of a classical statistical mechanical model of\\ncrystal melting, \
where the temperature is inverse of the string coupling\\nconstant. The \
crystal is a discretization of the toric base of the Calabi-Yau\\nwith \
lattice length $g_s$. As a strong evidence for this duality we recover \
the\\ntopological vertex in terms of the statistical mechanical \
probability\\ndistribution for crystal melting.\\n  We also propose a more \
general duality involving the dimer problem on\\nperiodic lattices and \
topological A-model string on arbitrary local toric\\nthreefolds. The $(p,q)$ \
5-brane web, dual to Calabi-Yau, gets identified with\\nthe transition \
regions of rigid dimer configurations.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
