                  "\"$G_2$ Manifolds, Mirror Symmetry and Geometric \
Engineering\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"comments\"", "\[Rule]", "\"35 pages, harvmac\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", "\"HUTP-01/A048\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We construct Calabi-Yau geometries with wrapped D6 \
branes which realize\\n${\\\\cal N}=1$ supersymmetric $A_r$ quiver theories, \
and study the corresponding\\ngeometric transitions. This also yields new \
large $N$ dualities for topological\\nstrings generalizing topological \
strings/large $N$ Chern-Simons duality.\\nLifting up to M-theory yields \
smooth quantum geometric transitions without\\nbranes or fluxes, in the \
context of $G_2$ holonomy manifolds. In addition we\\nconstruct a linear \
sigma model realization which is relevant for the worldsheet\\ntheory of \
superstrings propagating in local manifolds with $G_2$ holonomy, and\\nobtain \
mirror geometries for this class of supersymmetric sigma models.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
