added; final\\n  version to appear in Nuclear Physics B\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"journal-ref\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"Nucl.Phys. B473 (1996) 74-92\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"doi\"", "\[Rule]", "\"10.1016/0550-3213(96)00242-8\""}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"report-no\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"DUKE-TH-96-106, HUTP-96/A007\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"categories\"", "\[Rule]", "\"hep-th\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"license\"", "\[Rule]", "Null"}]}, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We study compactifications of F-theory on certain \
Calabi--Yau threefolds. We\\nfind that $N=2$ dualities of type II/heterotic \
strings in 4 dimensions get\\npromoted to $N=1$ dualities between heterotic \
string and F-theory in 6\\ndimensions. The six dimensional \
heterotic/heterotic duality becomes a classical\\ngeometric symmetry of the \
Calabi--Yau in the F-theory setup. Moreover the\\nF-theory compactification \
sheds light on the nature of the strong coupling\\ntransition and what lies \
beyond the transition at finite values of heterotic\\nstring coupling \
constant.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
