                RowBox[{
                 "\"license\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\""}]}\
, {
                
                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  D3-brane probes of exceptional Yukawa points in \
F-theory GUTs are natural\\nhidden sectors for particle phenomenology. We \
find that coupling the probe to\\nthe MSSM yields a new class of N = 1 \
conformal fixed points with computable\\ninfrared R-charges. Quite \
surprisingly, we find that the MSSM only weakly mixes\\nwith the strongly \
coupled sector in the sense that the MSSM fields pick up\\nsmall exactly \
computable anomalous dimensions. Additionally, we find that\\nalthough the \
states of the probe sector transform as complete GUT multiplets,\\ntheir \
coupling to Standard Model fields leads to a calculable \
threshold\\ncorrection to the running of the visible sector gauge couplings \
which improves\\nprecision unification. We also briefly consider scenarios in \
which SUSY is\\nbroken in the hidden sector. This leads to a gauge mediated \
spectrum for the\\ngauginos and first two superpartner generations, with \
additional contributions\\nto the third generation superpartners and Higgs \
sector.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
