                RowBox[{
                 "\"abstract\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  "\"  We make a number of conjectures about the geometry of \
continuous moduli\\nparameterizing the string landscape. In particular we \
conjecture that such\\nmoduli are always given by expectation value of scalar \
fields and that moduli\\nspaces with finite non-zero diameter belong to the \
swampland. We also\\nconjecture that points at infinity in a moduli space \
correspond to points where\\nan infinite tower of massless states appear, and \
that near these regions the\\nmoduli space is negatively curved. We also \
propose that there is no non-trivial\\n1-cycle of minimum length in the \
moduli space. This leads in particular to the\\nprediction of the existence \
of a radially massive partner to the axion. These\\nconjectures put strong \
constraints on inflaton potentials that can appear in a\\nconsistent quantum \
theory of gravity. Our conjectures are supported by a number\\nof highly \
non-trivial examples from string theory. Moreover it is shown that\\nthese \
conditions can be violated if gravity is decoupled.\\n\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"versions\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"version\"", "\[Rule]", "\"v1\""}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{
                    "\"created\"", "\[Rule]", 
                    "\"Fri, 26 May 2006 20:02:37 GMT\""}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"update_date\"", "\[Rule]", "\"2008-11-26\""}]}, {
                RowBox[{"\"authors_parsed\"", "\[Rule]", 
                  RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Ooguri\"", ",", "\"Hirosi\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"\"Vafa\"", ",", "\"Cumrun\"", ",", "\"\""}], 
                    "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}}, RowSpacings -> 1, ColumnAlignments -> 
              Left, ColumnAlignments -> Left], Column], 
            Function[BoxForm`e$, 
             TableForm[BoxForm`e$]]]],
          Annotation[#, 
           
           TableForm[{
            "id" -> "hep-th/0605264", "submitter" -> "Hirosi Ooguri", 
             "authors" -> "Hirosi Ooguri and Cumrun Vafa", "title" -> 
             "On the Geometry of the String Landscape and the Swampland", 
             "comments" -> "18 pages", "journal-ref" -> 
             "Nucl.Phys.B766:21-33,2007", "doi" -> 
             "10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.10.033", "report-no" -> 
             "CALT-68-2600, HUTP-06/A017", "categories" -> "hep-th", 
             "license" -> Null, "abstract" -> 
             "  We make a number of conjectures about the geometry of \
continuous moduli\nparameterizing the string landscape. In particular we \
conjecture that such\nmoduli are always given by expectation value of scalar \
fields and that moduli\nspaces with finite non-zero diameter belong to the \
swampland. We also\nconjecture that points at infinity in a moduli space \
correspond to points where\nan infinite tower of massless states appear, and \
that near these regions the\nmoduli space is negatively curved. We also \
propose that there is no non-trivial\n1-cycle of minimum length in the moduli \
space. This leads in particular to the\nprediction of the existence of a \
radially massive partner to the axion. These\nconjectures put strong \
constraints on inflaton potentials that can appear in a\nconsistent quantum \
theory of gravity. Our conjectures are supported by a number\nof highly \
non-trivial examples from string theory. Moreover it is shown that\nthese \
conditions can be violated if gravity is decoupled.\n", 
             "versions" -> {{
               "version" -> "v1", "created" -> 
                "Fri, 26 May 2006 20:02:37 GMT"}}, "update_date" -> 
             "2008-11-26", 
             "authors_parsed" -> {{"Ooguri", "Hirosi", ""}, {
               "Vafa", "Cumrun", ""}}}], "Tooltip"]& ], InsetBox[
